WEBVTT

00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:04.917
Can we maybe slow down?
There's no one even following us.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.667
Don't look back. Look up.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:13.625
I think we're about
to have some company.

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:15.458
-Stop the car.
-What?

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:16.375
-What?
-Stop!

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:19.292
Go, reverse!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.167
Laura, this is…

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.000
me.

00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:26.917
Hi.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.667
Parallel contact, babe?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.042
Well, you know, you've always said
that you wish you'd met me earlier.

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:33.042
Here I am.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.000
Do you remember this?

00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:42.875
I mean, if this is happening to me,
it already happened to you, right?

00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:45.792
Unless it works more
like a multiverse.

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.667
Each ripple creates
an alternate timeline.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.958
It's not a multiverse.

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:51.333
My God,
we watched too many movies.

00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:55.250
So 2050, is it really bad?

00:00:56.292 --> 00:00:57.625
-It's not great.
-Find him.

00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:01.583
Get ready to run.

00:01:18.708 --> 00:01:20.458
What is happening?!

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.333
You know what you have to do.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:28.458
Stop time travel
from ever being invented.

00:01:28.542 --> 00:01:29.375
Boom.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:31.625
What's your plan?

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.458
I'm not gonna explain my plan
to a 12-year-old nerd…

00:01:34.542 --> 00:01:37.500
-You don't have a plan.
-Because I don't have a plan, but…

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.083
I know somebody who does.

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:40.750
Dad.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.667
-I'm the godfather of time travel?
-The Adam Project.

00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:49.042
We don't pull this off,
we're not gettin' back.

00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:50.000
What do you say?

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.167
-Punch that sh--.
-Oh yeah.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.417
I spent 30 years

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.292
trying to get away
from the me that was you.

00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:14.292
And I'll tell you what.

00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:23.167
But you were the best part
all along.

00:02:25.792 --> 00:02:27.625
How'd you get to be so smart?

00:02:27.708 --> 00:02:29.458
How'd you get to be so dumb?

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:33.375
Nice try.

